ass='sig'>+0.16\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.10 to +0.22), about +2.2\u00b0F since 1886.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 5 of 12 months; January fell. Highs rose in 9 of 12 months.","t_rain":"San Antonio has gotten wetter","p_rain":"San Antonio's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.43 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.06 to +0.80), about +6.0 inches since 1886. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 32.4 inches a year. The wettest year was 1973 (52.28 in); the driest, 1917 (10.11 in). San Antonio almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.2 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 8 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}